 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to accept new public sanitary sewer mains, sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at West Campbell Road (unnumbered), also known as Days Valley Reserve (MWS Project No. 26-SL-131 and Proposal No. 2026M-079ES-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, the acceptance of approximately 822 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 118 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), seven sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at West Campbell Road (unnumbered), also known as Days Valley Reserve, is needed to construct Project No. 26SL131; and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2026M079ES-001 on September 1, 2026, for the acceptance of said sanitary sewer mains, sanitary sewer manholes and easements. \nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to accept approximately 822 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 118 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), seven sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at West Campbell Road (unnumbered), also known as Days Valley Reserve, as shown on Exhibit 1, which are attached hereto and incorporated by reference:\nMap & Parcel: \t\t\t\tAddress:\n03300010400\t\t\t\t\tWest Campbell Road (unnumbered)\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the acceptance authorized by this ordinance. \nSection 3.\tAmendments to this legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nSection 4.\tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it. \n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance accepts approximately 822 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 118 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), seven sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at West Campbell Road (unnumbered), also known as Days Valley Reserve.\n\nThis ordinance has been approved by the Planning Commission. Future amendments to this ordinance may be approved by resolution.\n\nFiscal Note: This ordinance has no cost to Metro. Donated easements have no market value according to the Department of Water Services.\n\n"
}
